      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix the outdated `ModelConfig.compute_hash()` docstring, which still describes the pre-#26468 opt-in hashing pattern. This is the remaining gap for #39479 TODO 8 (\"docstrings not up-to-date in the opt-out configs\"): it complements #46714 (docstrings in the opt-in configs) and #60739 (`CacheConfig`), with no overlap — neither open PR touches `vllm/config/model.py`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Rewrite the WARNING paragraph of `ModelConfig.compute_hash()` to the actual opt-out semantics: all dataclass fields are hashed by default; a new field only needs to be added to `ignored_factors` when it does NOT affect the computation graph.\n- Docstring-only change; no behavior change.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Verified against the implementation: `get_hash_factors()` in `vllm/config/utils.py` hashes every dataclass field not present in `ignored_factors`, and `ModelConfig.compute_hash()` uses exactly this pattern (in contrast to the opt-in `factors.append(...)` pattern still used by other config classes, whose docstrings remain accurate).\n- Duplicate-work check: `gh pr list --search \"39479 in:body\"`, `\"compute_hash docstring\"`, `\"ignored_factors doc\"` — no open PR modifies the `ModelConfig.compute_hash()` docstring.\n- `pre-commit run --files vllm/config/model.py` — all hooks pass.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: #26468 migrated `ModelConfig.compute_hash()` to the opt-out `get_hash_factors(self, ignored_factors)` pattern, but the docstring's WARNING was left describing the old opt-in pattern (\"ensure that it is included in the factors list if it affects the computation graph\"). A contributor following the old text would believe new fields must be manually registered to affect the hash, when in fact every field is hashed by default — the only required action is the opposite one: excluding non-graph-affecting fields via `ignored_factors`.\n\nAI assistance was used (Kimi Code); every changed line was reviewed and verified by the human submitter.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
